        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Tute arrastrado',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Tute arrastrado is a Tute variant for three or four players (with four, the dealer sits out each hand). Thirteen cards each from a 40-card Spanish pack; last card turned for trump. Follow suit and overtake or trump; after winning a trick you may sing 20 or 40 (40 before 20); tute (four kings or four horses) wins the hand outright. Chip payments: 100 or 200 from each opponent, plus 40 or 20 per declaration.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Tute originated in Italy as tutti and spread to Spain in the 19th century, becoming one of the country's most popular card games. Tute arrastrado is an individual-play variant for three or four players (with four, the dealer sits out each hand), using the same 40-card Spanish pack and marriage-type scoring; it appears alongside other Tute variants such as corriente, habanero, and subastado in Spanish card-game literature.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Three players, or four with dealer sitting out each hand.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '40-card Spanish pack.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Thirteen cards each, one at a time; last card turned for trump.',
              },
